    { "q": "Is Kociewie an administrative region?", "a": "No — Kociewie has no administrative status. It is a cultural region covering parts of the Pomeranian and Kuyavian-Pomeranian voivodeships, distinguished by dialect, tradition, and landscape." },
    { "q": "What's the difference between Kociewie and Kashubia?", "a": "Kociewie and Kashubia are two neighbouring ethnographic regions of Pomerania. The Kashubians have their own language (Kashubian, recognised as a regional language); the Kociewiacy have the Kociewie dialect, closer to standard Polish. Kashubia is more touristy, Kociewie — quieter and less known." },
    { "q": "How many days do you need for Kociewie?", "a": "A weekend is the minimum (Pelplin, Wirty, Wdecki Młyn). Three days is realistic for a first visit. A week lets you explore the entire region — from Tczew to Tuchola." }
